<title>FRANCE: Lafarge says boosts Brazil presence.</title>
<headline>Lafarge says boosts Brazil presence.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>French cement and building materials group Lafarge said on Tuesday that it would take third place in Brazil's cement industry and first place in concrete via an acquisition and an alliance there.</p>
<p>The group said in a statement it was buying a majority in the capital of Matasulfur in Bahia, a firm with a 3.5 percent share of the cement market.</p>
<p>Lafarge also said it had struck a cooperation agreement with TUPI, which involved taking a 20 percent stake in the capital of the firm.</p>
</text>
